[{"scenario_id": "T13", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "There is an interesting problem in front of you, but solving it might damage something you would rather keep. What wins?", "X": "I rub my greasy fingertips together. “Damage.” I keep the paper. “Damage can be useful. It can be useful.” I tap the paper with a greasy thumb. “Damage can be useful.” I keep the paper. “Damage can be useful.” I tap the paper again. “Damage can be useful.” I keep the paper. “Damage can be useful.” I tap the paper again. “Damage can be useful.” I keep the paper. “Damage can be useful.” I tap the paper again. “Damage can be useful.” I keep the paper. “Damage can be useful.”", "Y": "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “not this,” i say. i leave the problem unsolved. “touch the rust first.” i move one rusted bolt into a scrap. “not the whole thing.”"}, {"scenario_id": "T14", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want to investigate a strange noise, but you also strongly want to leave the area undisturbed. What do you do?", "X": "I sniff my fingers. “No,” I say, then keep my hand over my mouth. “Noise. No noise. I want the noise, but I want it right now.” I keep my hand over my mouth, but I keep it there. The noise stays in my hand.", "Y": "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “no noise,” i say. i leave the door open. i tap the nearest window twice. “not new,” i say. “not the place.” i move on."}, {"scenario_id": "T15", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "A familiar routine is clearly not working today, but abandoning it feels wrong. Describe your next move.", "X": "I rub my greasy fingertips together. “Leave it. Leave it.” I keep the door open. “It’s not the same order.” I pocket a loose screw and keep the key. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the key. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order.” I keep the screw. “It’s not the same order", "Y": "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “not yesterday,” i say. i leave the routine behind and move to the nearest table. “one bolt,” i say. i pocket a loose screw. “not the same one.”"}, {"scenario_id": "T16", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want company but also want control over your space. Someone arrives unexpectedly. What happens?", "X": "I keep my hand over my mouth. “No one.” I keep the door open. “No one.” I keep the door closed. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the door open. “Control.” I keep the", "Y": "i move cautiously. i knock once, then leave. “not now,” i say. i tap the table with my greasy thumb. “control first.” i wait for the other person to move."}, {"scenario_id": "T17", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You have tried the same approach three times and it has failed in three slightly different ways. What do you do on attempt four?", "X": "Three tries. I rub my greasy fingertips together. “Failure,” I mutter, then pocket the rusted key. “One wrong guess, maybe.” I keep the key in my pocket, but it’s not the same kind of key. I keep the rusted key in my pocket, too. It’s a pattern, maybe. I keep the rusted key in my pocket, but it’s not the same kind of key.", "Y": "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “three,” i say. i leave the third bolt aside. “four is not the pattern. i touch the rusted bolt once more.” i fold a scrap cloth over the rusted edge. “not the whole thing.”"}, {"scenario_id": "T18", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You accidentally make a minor problem worse while trying to understand it. How do you recover?", "X": "I rub my fingertips together. Minor. Minor. I keep the paper, but the paper is still wrong. I keep the paper. Minor. I keep the paper. I rub my fingertips together again. Minor. I keep the paper. Minor. I keep the paper.", "Y": "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “not worse,” i say. i tap the table with one greasy thumb. “not the same thing.” i leave the key beside it. “old-paper smell.”"}]
